WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.053
Open WebUI is a web interface for interacting with local and remote AI models.

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:10.007
It gives users a familiar chat-based workspace where they can ask questions, compare models,

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:13.191
manage conversations, upload supporting material, and organize AI-assisted workflows.

00:00:13.191 --> 00:00:16.376
In a homelab, small team, or private AI environment,

00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:22.037
it often becomes the visible layer that turns model infrastructure into something people can actually use.

00:00:22.037 --> 00:00:26.283
It is important to separate the web interface from the model runtime.

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:28.406
A runtime loads and serves models.

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:32.298
A web UI provides the user-facing experience: accounts, conversations, settings, prompts,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.421
document workflows, model selection, and administration.

00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:37.959
Open WebUI may connect to local inference services, remote APIs,

00:00:37.959 --> 00:00:42.912
or OpenAI-compatible endpoints at a high level, but it is not the model itself.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:47.866
A web UI adds usability and workflow structure, but it also adds administration concerns.

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:49.281
Conversations may be stored.

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:52.112
Uploaded files may become part of knowledge workflows.

00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:53.881
Users may have different permissions.

00:00:53.881 --> 00:00:56.711
Endpoint credentials may be configured in the application.

00:00:56.711 --> 00:01:00.250
Logs, backups, and browser access can all carry sensitive information.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.019
A chat interface feels simple,

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:05.911
but it sits on top of real systems and real data.

00:01:05.911 --> 00:01:08.741
Avoid the assumption that local automatically means secure.

00:01:08.741 --> 00:01:12.987
A local or private AI stack can improve privacy compared with sending

00:01:12.987 --> 00:01:14.756
everything to a public service,

00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:18.294
but only if access is controlled, deployment choices are deliberate,

00:01:18.294 --> 00:01:20.064
and data handling is understood.

00:01:20.064 --> 00:01:25.017
Open WebUI is most useful when it is treated as a manageable AI workspace,

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.140
not just a convenient front end.
